ez: Good. Decision: TAP and Iberia go to a group-fare request, Vueling is out. Mei, can you draft the flight hold request this week and share it for review by Friday?\n[2026-04-29T10:36:00Z] Mei Tanaka: Will do. I'll have it in the shared folder by end of day Friday.\n[2026-04-29T10:36:00Z] Sofia Alvarez: Perfect. Item two — room allocation. I want to land on a number today. Daniel, what's your read?\n[2026-04-29T10:37:00Z] Daniel Okafor: I've been going back and forth. Anything under seven rooms per city and we're cramming families into triples; anything over nine and we're paying for rooms nobody sleeps in. I'd land at eight. Enough for every family to have their own space, small enough that if a hotel falls through we can rebook without it being a scramble.\n[2026-04-29T10:38:00Z] Mei Tanaka: I'd second eight. And on which blocks — I'd suggest we use the Porto room block and the Seville room block we already have quotes on. Two reasons: those are the two cities where hotels sell out first in July, so locking them early matters most there, and they're both sized such that eight rooms fits cleanly without splitting us across two hotels.\n[2026-04-29T10:39:00Z] Sofia Alvarez: That works for me. Any concern about Lisbon if we only lock those two blocks now?\n[2026-04-29T10:39:00Z] Daniel Okafor: Some, but Lisbon has more inventory. I think the trade-off is worth it. We can finalize Lisbon once flights are held.\n[2026-04-29T10:40:00Z] Sofia Alvarez: Okay. Decision: eight rooms each in the Porto room block and the Seville room block, with a 4-week window for families to confirm their room preferences. Daniel, you'll own the room allocation?\n[2026-04-29T10:40:00Z] Daniel Okafor: Yep.\n[2026-04-29T10:41:00Z] Sofia Alvarez: Good. Item three — the deposit budget. Rob confirmed the $48k pot is fully collected. Mei, how do we want to slice it?\n[2026-04-29T10:41:00Z] Mei Tanaka: I'd carve out $31k for flights, $13k for lodging — the Porto and Seville blocks plus the Lisbon