ocation, trip cost sheet update today, transfers booking with Rob. Me: I'll update Rob and Leila on the carrier decision and the dates. Anything I'm missing?\n[2026-04-29T10:50:00Z] Mei Tanaka: I think that covers it.\n[2026-04-29T10:50:00Z] Daniel Okafor: One thing — do we want to set a regular check-in between now and Jun 8? I'd suggest weekly for the next few weeks given how much we have to lock down.\n[2026-04-29T10:51:00Z] Sofia Alvarez: Good call. Same time next Wednesday, and I'll keep this slot held through Jun 3.\n[2026-04-29T10:51:00Z] Daniel Okafor: Works.\n[2026-04-29T10:51:00Z] Mei Tanaka: Works.\n[2026-04-29T10:52:00Z] Sofia Alvarez: One more thing while I have you both — on the itinerary itself, are we still aligned that the group booking is the core Lisbon, Porto, Seville route, and any side trips are optional add-ons each family books on their own? I don't want the group booking to sprawl before we've locked the core.\n[2026-04-29T10:53:00Z] Mei Tanaka: Aligned. Core route only for the group booking. Side trips are on each family.\n[2026-04-29T10:53:00Z] Daniel Okafor: Same.\n[2026-04-29T10:54:00Z] Sofia Alvarez: Great. And on the document checklist — passport validity, entry authorization, and proof of cover under the Allianz Travel group policy. Anything else you want on there?\n[2026-04-29T10:55:00Z] Mei Tanaka: I'd add a quick contact form due with the checklist — just three things, an emergency contact, a mobile number that works abroad, and any seating or room requests.\n[2026-04-29T10:55:00Z] Daniel Okafor: Plus one on that. Easy to collect, useful.\n[2026-04-29T10:56:00Z] Sofia Alvarez: Added. So the checklist: passport validity, entry authorization, insurance cover, and the contact form. Mei, please add those to the trip brief.\n[2026-04-29T10:56:00Z] Mei Tanaka: Will do.\n[2026-04-29T10:57:00Z] Sofia Alvarez: Okay — anything else for either of you before I let you go?\n[2026-04-29T10:57:00Z] Daniel Okafor: Nothing from me.\n[2026-04-29T10: